   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "Yes, `list` follows the ISO-8601 rule.\n\n- **Printing:** `fieldnotes/cli.py:21` prints `note['created']` as it is stored. It does no date formatting of its own.\n- **Storage:** `fieldnotes/store.py:24` writes `created` with `moment.isoformat()`. The moment is timezone-aware UTC, so the output looks like `2026-01-02T03:04:05+00:00`.\n- **Other date output:** nothing else in `fieldnotes/` formats dates. `add` prints only the note text.\n\n**Weak spot:** `list` prints whatever string is in `notes.json`. It never checks or normalizes it. A note written by hand or by an older version in a non-ISO format would be printed unchanged. That doesn't happen with the current code. If you want it enforced, `list` could parse each value with `datetime.fromisoformat` and re-emit it with `isoformat()`. I haven't changed anything.",
   "suspended": false
